UID:9daa178948f37fbb412d19fa7060612b10312026_10:44:43_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Sealed Off
LOCATION:Crescent Underground, Morse and Stiles Colleges, 304 York Street, New Haven, United States
URL:https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2337660
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable evening of theater at the Yale Vermilion Theater FA26 Showcase! \n\nSet in 1940s Shanghai, Sealed Off begins when a sudden military blockade brings a tram to a halt amid the turmoil of a city at war. Two strangers, Wu Cuiyuan, a university English teaching assistant, and Lü Zongzhen, a bank clerk, find themselves together in the crowded tram. She longs for genuine human contact; he seeks an escape from the monotony of everyday life. As their conversation unfolds, two individuals constrained by family, society, and the roles they are expected to play discover the possibility of connection in this fleeting moment of stillness. But when the blockade is lifted and the tram begins moving again, what will become of them?\n\nAdapted from Eileen Chang's short story of the same name, Sealed Off explores the delicate interplay between truth and illusion in human nature through a chance encounter between two strangers. It also raises questions about the complexities of love: Do we truly fall in love with another person, or do we simply long to be seen through their eyes? Amid the many constraints of reality, can we ever truly reach our authentic selves and one another?\n\nThis production is supported by the Grace Hopper College Creative and Performing Arts Award. Production in Chinese (Mandarin) with English subtitles. The event is open to the public, with donations welcome (via Venmo @ChinYuan-Ong). We can’t wait to see you there!\n---\nEvent Details: https://yaleconnect.yale.edu/rsvp?id=2337660
END:VEVENT
